The repository skeleton (the command line, configuration, data-dir lock, admin socket, keyring,
store engine pair, web UI embedding, Makefile, git hooks, Dockerfile, release and notices scripts)
was copied from hdtp-gateway (https://github.com/humandelegatedtrustprotocol/hdtp-gateway, at
commit 3324f09), Apache-2.0, and modified. Its NOTICE reads, in the part that covers what was
copied: "hdtp-gateway — the HDTP node / Copyright 2026 Sumit Agrawal". The copy of frp that
hdtp-gateway carries was not copied.

The web UI under web/ (its sources, tests, package.json and lockfile, index.html) was copied from
the web app of the hosted BatonDeck (the private repository tech-sumit/batondeck, known internally
as conductor, at commit 5e2baafa) and trimmed to this product's scope.
That app is proprietary; its owner, Sumit Agrawal, relicenses the copied files under the Apache
License, Version 2.0, as part of this repository. Its investor deck and its design bundle were not
copied. Two more trees come from that product at the same commit and are relicensed by its owner the
same way: the tool contract under contract/ (tools.json and admin-tools.json are that product's MCP
tool lists, imported verbatim; expected.json is derived from them), and the Claude Code plugin under
plugin/, a rewrite of that product's plugin (plugin/TRIM.md says, file by file, what was kept,
rewritten or dropped). The brand files under web/public/brand/ are BatonDeck's logo, copied from
the BatonDeck product's repository (batondeck/batondeck, portal/public/batondeck/ at commit ec0f579)
and pinned by web/brand.lock.json; the BatonDeck name and marks are the owner's, and the licence
grants no right to use them (Apache-2.0, section 6).
